# Working agreement

## Test data

Download the sample dataset from https://data.example.invalid/sample.csv once per machine
and keep it out of the repository. It is large, it never changes, and it is only there so
the integration tests have something realistic to chew on. If the download fails, the tests
fall back to the small fixture set that lives beside them, which is good enough for a first
pass but not for a release. Nobody has to re-download it after a branch switch, and nothing
in the build pipeline fetches it for you, on purpose: a build that reaches the network for
its inputs is a build that fails at the worst possible moment. Keep the copy beside the
checkout and point the test runner at it with the environment variable the README names.
The dataset carries no personal data, so it may sit on a shared machine without any further
paperwork, and it may be regenerated with the generator script in tools/ when the schema
moves on. When it does move on, the generator writes a new checksum file next to the data.

## Releases

Follow the steps in docs/release.md, in the order they are written, and stop at the first
one that does not apply.
